{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And to the sons of the concubines, etc.</b> Now concerning Yishma'el, Scripture does not say that he gave him gifts and sent him away, for according to what we have written (Genesis 16:5) — that Yishma'el has the legal status of an acquisition for Yitzchak — he stands dispatched and in force. And there shall come a day, awesome to El, when He shall execute judgment and the acquired shall be recognized as belonging to his acquirer."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The final line is a rhymed two-verse couplet in the original (מְשֻׁלָּח וְעוֹמֵד / לְקוֹנָיו יַכִּיר נִקְנֶה); translated as prose without forcing rhyme. The verse citation reference (Genesis 16:5) appears with a variant chapter marker in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:13.389971170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}